---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Tamio Privacy Policy — Oksyderkeis" description="Privacy policy for the Tamio personal finance app.">
  <main class="px-5 py-16 max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-invert">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> August 8, 2026</p>

    <p>
      Tamio is a personal finance app designed to help you organize your money with more clarity.
      This policy explains what data Tamio uses, why it uses it, and how you can control or delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Data We Process</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Email address for account creation and sign-in.</li>
      <li>Finance entries you add inside the app, such as expenses, budgets, investments, shopping items, and coupons.</li>
      <li>Optional notification preferences.</li>
      <li>Optional location access only for nearby coupon alerts when you enable it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. What We Do With That Data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Show your financial data back to you inside the app.</li>
      <li>Generate reminders and coupon notifications when you enable them.</li>
      <li>Let you export your own data.</li>
      <li>Protect account access and keep your app experience working correctly.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. What We Do Not Do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We do not sell your personal data.</li>
      <li>We do not share your finance entries with advertisers.</li>
      <li>We do not use your data to give financial advice.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Storage and Security</h2>
    <p>
      Tamio stores account and app data through Supabase infrastructure hosted in the EU.
      Access is protected with authenticated access controls and row-level security so each user can only access their own data.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Location and Notifications</h2>
    <p>
      Location access is optional. If you enable it, Tamio uses it only to detect when you are near stores that match your saved coupons or deals.
      Notifications are also optional and can be turned off from the Profile section at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>
      If you are in the EU, you can request access, correction, export, or deletion of your data.
      You can also delete your account directly from the Tamio profile screen.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions or data requests, contact:<br />
      <strong>david@oksyderkeis.net</strong>
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This policy may be updated when the app changes. The latest published version on this page is the version that applies.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>

